### Unit problems verified from data (metadata is wrong)
1. Height 1981 is NOT inches: raw 400-611 and count(inches-part > 11) == 0 -> feet*100+inches.
   Conversion (h//100)*12 + h%100 -> min 48, median 67, max 83, mean 67.01 in; corr with height 1985 = 0.934;
   slope 0.945; sex means M 69.82 / F 64.18 vs 1985 M 70.02 / F 64.23.
2. Weights are NOT kg: range 50-393 (means 145-168) -> pounds. Hence BMI = 703*lb/in^2.
   Wrong scaling (/10) gives mean BMI 38.0 (implausible); correct gives:
   BMI1981 22.67 (sd 3.58), BMI1989 25.15 (sd 6.42), BMI1992 26.12 (sd 5.26); 0.2-0.7% outside 15-45.

## Confounders kept
- Age of respondent 1979 (0% missing, 14-22); Age 1989 (missing 2081) optional
- Sex 1979 (6403 M / 6283 F); Racial/ethnic cohort 1979 (3=7510, 2=3174, 1=2002)
- ASVAB AR/WK/PC/MK 1981 (~12% missing; scale 165-825, mean ~473 -> re-standardise, average 4)
- Parental SES: mother grade 1979 (missing 808), father grade 1979 (missing 1806);
  occupation of adult male at 14 (missing 3874) is a 3-digit census occupation CODE -> optional major-group dummies
- Family size 1979 (0% missing)
- Baseline BMI 1989 (and 1981) = most important control (reverse causality / secular trend)
- Sensitivity only (collider risk): own income 1989 (31% missing), wealth 1990 (27% missing), own grade 1979 (max 95 -> 2 implausible)
- Dropped: residence-type year panels (7189 missing in 1981), convicted (11938) / sentenced (9937) missing, class rank (~55%)

## Sample sizes for the planned analysis
- exposure + BMI1992: 8503
- + baseline BMI1989 + all covariates listwise: 6563
Unadjusted BMI1992 means by savings code: put-in 25.43 (2272) < took-out 26.15 (2462) ~ no-change 26.17 (1270) < no-savings 26.74 (2499)

## Proposed design
Exposure: patience index 3/2/1/0 (put-in / no-change / took-out / no-savings); binary saver; drop no-savings sensitivity.
Outcome: BMI 1992. Model: OLS HC1 with sex, race, age79, baseline BMI1989, ASVAB avg, mother+father grade (+family size);
log-BMI and obesity(>=30) logistic; sex-stratified. Missing: required exposure+outcome, median imputation + indicators;
listwise and MICE(5) as sensitivity. Direction reported as impatience -> BMI (expect positive).
